- Add expiry payouts, off by default with `expiry_payouts`
  In expiry payout mode the server records an owner mailbox key `M` for
  every VTXO, and the watchman pays the VTXOs of an expired tree to
  `tr(M)` instead of to the operator. The fee is the higher of 2,000 sats
  and 1% of the value of the owner in the tree, once for each owner in each
  tree. The mode is fixed when the database is created. Without it, the
  server behaves as upstream. See `docs/expiry-payouts.md`.
  [#1](https://github.com/SatoshiPortal/scuttle/pull/1)
  - `watchman.expiry_payout_max_fee_rate` caps the feerate of a payout
    transaction and of its replacements.
  - `ln_receive_ark_address_hints` lets a receiver put its Ark address in
    the route hints of an invoice, so a payer on this server pays the invoice
    with an arkoor.
